I have done so formerly but changed my strategy WRT potions and corpses;
the potions are IMO better used for alchemy and to escape specific levels
during the home-run. Wraith corpses I usually eat, but they are rare if
you are looking outside morgues for them. And on a morgue level (Valley,
specifically) they leave corpses only with a very reduced probability[*];
so, for example, if I am equipped with one or more pet purple worms, they
will get the wraiths for instant and guaranteed level gain. In consequence
wraiths are able to kill everything including a multiple times resurrected
high-level Wizard. Using potions and wraiths that way was a fruitful change
in my games.

